```
Note stateToQuery skips values equal to defaults; view: split is the default so it's omitted. 

9. `applyView()` calls `applyMode(state.view)` which on activation calls resize + showYear. But resize() sets `state.view` if null using `currentViewFromState()`; fine.

10. `showYear` calls `store.update({year})` — if called from the store subscription for `year` change, this writes the sanitised same value; store.update with identical value → sanitise same → maybe no notify; check store.update implementation to ensure no infinite loop. Let me look at update() code.

11. `renderTimeline()` reads `store.getState().year` and `state.loadedYear`; called from loadIndex before showYear sets loadedYear — `nearestSnapshot` fallback works.

12. In `loadSnapshot`, `state.loadingYear !== entry.year` guard prevents repeated loading messages; minor.

13. `showYear`: `if (pushHistory) ... else if (store.getState().year !== year) store.update({ year })` — simplify to always `store.update({year})` when different. Remove the pushHistory param (unused).

14. The `yearInput.value = formatYear(year)` sets e.g. "1900 CE" — then submit parses fine.

15. `hover` element: `el('p', {..., hidden: true})` — dom.el probably sets attributes; `hidden: true` may set attribute `hidden="true"` which works. Let me check dom.el implementation.

16. `el('option', { value: '' }, text)` — need to confirm el handles props like `value`/`checked`/`disabled`. Let me read dom.js.

17. `politySelect.replaceChildren(...options)` — each option created via el; fine.

18. `searchResults.replaceChildren(el('li', ...))` with `el('li', {}, text)`.

19. `canvas.setPointerCapture` — fine.

20. Mode bar in main: my CSS must style and ensure `#main` layout. Note: `main` has class `zh-shell app-main`. `.app-modebar` inside; CSS rule display flex.

21. `applyMode`: hide/show. Since the section is created with `hidden: true` and main.js init runs while view=split, good.

22. Canvas size: `mapwrap.getBoundingClientRect()` may be 0 when hidden; resize runs after activation (requestAnimationFrame) — but if the section is hidden and CSS `display:none`, rect = 0 → width fallback 320. When activated we call resize again. Good. But CSS: `section[hidden]` must be `display:none` — browsers handle `hidden` by default unless overridden by `display:flex` etc. My CSS must not set display on the section without `[hidden]{display:none}` override. I'll add `[hidden]{display:none !important}` guard in history.css for my elements.

23. `context.setTransform(ratio,0,0,ratio,0,0)` then draw with CSS pixel coordinates. Note `clearRect(0,0,width,height)` in CSS px after transform — fine.

24. The label candidate uses `feature.labelRing.areaPx(state.view, state.size)` where areaPx uses `projectPoint` (no offset) — fine for area magnitude but for wrapped features could be off; acceptable.

25. `drawLabels(visible, offsets)`: offsets unused; remove param.

26. Ring label anchor: `ringAnchor` at ring bbox midpoint — for wrapped features might place label off-screen; we skip if outside.

27. `state.index.repository` link etc.

28. `updateSourceNote` uses `index.coverage.firstYear`.

29. Module top-level: `init(ctx)` only. The import of `store.js` is fine in Node (it's DOM-free). Tests can import history.js without DOM because top-level only defines functions/constants. Yes.

30. `export function init` returns object — main.js expects API.

Let me fix all these issues by rewriting parts of the file. Given the number of fixes, I'll do targeted edits.

Also check dom.js `el` signature.

